  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c911",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1833,
      "bookHadithIndex": 51,
      "text": "It was narrated that:Jabir bin Abdullah said: “The Messenger of Allah said: 'A Wasq is sixty Sa.' ”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1833-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1833-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1833-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1833-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c912",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1834,
      "bookHadithIndex": 52,
      "text": "It was narrated that:Zainab, the wife of Abdullah said: “I asked the Messenger of Allah: 'Will it be accepted as charity on my part if I spend on my husband and the orphans in my care?' The Messenger of Allah said: 'She will have two rewards, the reward for charity and the reward for upholding ties of kinship.'”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1834-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1834-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1834-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1834-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c913",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1835,
      "bookHadithIndex": 53,
      "text": "It was narrated that:Umm Salamah said: “The Messenger of Allah enjoined charity upon us. Zainab, the wife of Abdullah said: 'Will it be accepted as charity on my part if I give charity to my husband who is poor, and to the children of a brother of mine who are orphans, spending such and such on them, and in all circumstances?' He said: 'Yes.'”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1835-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1835-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1835-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1835-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c914",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1836,
      "bookHadithIndex": 54,
      "text": "It was narrated from Hisham bin Urwah, from his father, that:his grandfather said: “The Messenger of Allah said: 'If one of you were to take his rope (or ropes) and go to the mountains, and bring a bundle of firewood on his back to sell, and thus become independent of means, that would be better for him than begging from people who may either give him something or not give him anything.'”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1836-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih Hadith"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1836-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1836-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1836-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c915",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1837,
      "bookHadithIndex": 55,
      "text": "Abdur-Rahman bin Yazid narrated that:Thawban said: “The Messenger of Allah said: 'Who will commit himself to one thing, I will guarantee him paradise?' I said: 'I will.' He said: 'Do not ask people for anything.' So Thawban would drop his whip while he was on his mount, and he would not say to anyone: 'Get that for me' rather he would dismount and grab it.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1837-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1837-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1837-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c916",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1838,
      "bookHadithIndex": 56,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that:the Messenger of Allah(ﷺ) said: “Whoever begs from people so as to accumulate more riches, he is asking for alive coal from hell, so let him ask for a lot or a little.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1838-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1838-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1838-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1838-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c917",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1839,
      "bookHadithIndex": 57,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: “Charity is not permissible for a rich person, or for one who is strong and healthy. ”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1839-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1839-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1839-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1839-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c918",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1840,
      "bookHadithIndex": 58,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: “Whoever begs when he has enough to suffice him, his begging will come on the Day of Resurrection like lacerations on his face. ” It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is sufficient for him?” He said: “Fifty Dirham or their value in gold.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1840-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1840-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1840-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c919",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1841,
      "bookHadithIndex": 59,
      "text": "Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: “Charity is not permissible for a rich man except in five cases: One who is appointed to collect it, a warrior fighting in the cause of Allah, a rich man who buys it with his own money, a poor man who receives the charity and gives it as a gift to a rich man, and a debtor.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1841-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1841-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1841-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c91a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1842,
      "bookHadithIndex": 60,
      "text": "Sa'eed bin Yasar narrated that:he heard Abu Hurairah say: “The Messenger of Allah said: 'No one gives charity from good sources - for Allah does not accept anything but that which is good - but the Most Merciful takes it in His right hand, even if it is a date, and it flourishes in the Hand of the Most Merciful until it becomes bigger than a mountain and he tends it as anyone of you would tend to his colt (i.e., young pony) or his young (weaned) camel.'”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1842-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1842-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1842-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c91b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1843,
      "bookHadithIndex": 61,
      "text": "Adi bin Hatim narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: “Each one of you will be spoken to by his lord, with no mediator between them. He will look in from of him and the fire will be facing him. He will look to his right and will not see anything but something that he had sent on before. He will look to his left and will not see anything but something that he had sent on before. Whoeever among you can save himself in Fire, even with half a date, let him do so.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1843-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1843-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1843-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1843-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c859dd1a4c9c86f0c91c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 8,
      "hadithIndex": 1844,
      "bookHadithIndex": 62,
      "text": "Salman bin Amir Dabbi narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: “Charity given to the poor is charity, and that given to a relative is two things: charity and upholding the ties of kinship.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1844-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1844-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1844-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-8-1844-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}